      ":question/id": "d36ecf41-14d3-5c33-b433-31e0dcd3d9be",
      ":question/problem": "If $P$ is a $12\\times 9$ matrix that has $4$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{rank}(P)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\text{rank}(P)$ is the number of pivot columns in $P.$ \n\nSince $P$ has $9$ columns and $4$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $P$ is \n\n$$\n9-4=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(P)=5.$"
